{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>On the corner tassels, a thread.</b> That it must be twisted, and our Rabbis of blessed memory also said: tzitzit — one third winding and two thirds loose threads. And the reason, as we say in the Midrash: the eight threads of tzitzit correspond to the eight things in the heart; or alternatively, the heart has eight names, and the heart is suspended at one third of a person's body, and therefore the threads begin from the first third and extend to two thirds, just as from the heart to the end of a person's body is two thirds. — Maharam."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:31.039000384Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}